meta {
  name: 07. Upload Settlement Receipt
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/attachments/upload
  body: multipartForm
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  file: @file()
  type: SETTLEMENT_RECEIPT
  group_id: {{settlementGroupId}}
  is_public: false
}

docs {
  # Upload Settlement Receipt

  POST /api/v1/attachments/upload is the existing shared upload endpoint, not a new settlement route. Bearer token required. Select a file in Body; Bruno supplies the multipart boundary.

  Form: file (required image or PDF, at most 10 MiB), type=SETTLEMENT_RECEIPT, optional group_id (ACTIVE or SETTLING group with active caller membership), is_public=false (always enforced even if true submitted). Do not send settlement_id or expense_id: binding is only through Create Settlement. Uploader account must be ACTIVE.

  Success: 201 with the shared AttachmentResponse (id, uploaded_by_user_id, optional group_id, type, original_filename, object_key, mime_type, file_size_bytes, file_hash, optional dimensions, is_public=false, access_url and timestamps). settlement_id is omitted until bound. The upload itself is visible only to its uploader. Copy data.id to settlementAttachmentIds, for example [1201]; variables are manual.

  Example response (hash/signature illustrative):

  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": {
      "id": 1201,
      "uploaded_by_user_id": 3,
      "group_id": 10,
      "type": "SETTLEMENT_RECEIPT",
      "original_filename": "receipt.pdf",
      "object_key": "attachments/settlement_receipt/3/2026/11/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001_receipt.pdf",
      "mime_type": "application/pdf",
      "file_size_bytes": 1000,
      "file_hash": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
      "is_public": false,
      "access_url": "https://storage.example.com/receipt?X-Amz-Signature=example",
      "uploaded_at": "2026-11-18T10:00:00Z",
      "created_at": "2026-11-18T10:00:00Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-18T10:00:00Z"
    }
  }
  ```

  Existing presigned upload/confirm routes also support this type. Confirm validates actual MIME/size and creates a fresh immutable storage object; use the returned attachment ID, not the original upload object key, for settlement linking. A stale PUT URL cannot modify the confirmed receipt. URLs must not be shared beyond their allowed viewers.

  Errors: 400 BAD_REQUEST (missing file, invalid form or direct link IDs), 400 INVALID_FILE_TYPE, 400 GROUP_INVALID_STATUS (supplied group CLOSED), 401 token errors, 403 USER_INACTIVE, 403 GROUP_FORBIDDEN, 404 GROUP_NOT_FOUND, 413 FILE_TOO_LARGE, 500 INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, 503 STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE. See shared attachment docs for the standard code/error envelope.
}
